Third-party map data, excluded from the above:

The Software contains map data from the sources below, and fetches, caches,
generates and exports more of it when it runs. Map data from these sources is
not covered by the proprietary terms above, wherever it is found:

- in the source tree: every file under src/app/maps/, whatever it is named;
- in data the Software fetches or caches while it runs; and
- in any map, scenario or other file the Software generates or exports.

In a generated or exported file, only the map data is excluded. Everything
else in it (the scenario, the forces, the orders) stays under whatever terms
otherwise apply to it.

The sources, and the terms their data comes under:

- OpenStreetMap. Data © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open
  Database License (ODbL) v1.0,
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/ — see
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. That data, and any database derived
  from it, may be used under the ODbL.
- Elevation. Data from the AWS Terrain Tiles (courtesy of Mapzen), derived from
  NASA SRTM, which is public domain. Attribution:
  "Terrain Tiles courtesy of Mapzen; elevation data from SRTM (NASA)".

The Software keeps these attributions with the data: on every map it draws,
and inside every file it exports.

